{"version":1,"content":"<html><body><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://pro-img-cdn.tvb.com/uploads/image/2026/10/2026yjYlhYYHdw1792682936.jpg?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1200\"/><p>法國發現全球首宗人類感染沙門達病毒死亡個案。</p><p></p><p>據報沙門達病毒主要透過，刺吸式蠓蟲叮咬傳播，常見於家牛，但亦曾在馬匹、羊駝、綿羊和山羊體內檢測到，目前並無這種病毒的商業疫苗。</p><p></p><p>法國衞生當局周四證實，一名患者本月早前死亡懷疑生前在東部地區被蠓蟲叮咬。法國傳媒報道，死者六十多歲，住在里昂。</p><p></p><p>當局稱未對公眾構成危險，世衞亦稱這是個別病例，不太可能進一步擴散。</p></body></html>","scraped_at":"2026-10-22T18:01:20.601959+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":176,"images":1,"source":"TVB 新聞","fallback":"none","origin":"article-html","completeness":"extracted"},"published_at":"2026-10-22T13:51:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-23T03:18:07.105475+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-10-22T17:58:06.278146+00:00","content_hash":"fc612fda3b6a84af835f5b8a749facc9f2372b1f456efb789f89ffb7b2b0221b","evidence_status":"full","scrape_error":null,"content_retention":{"scraped_at":"2026-10-22T18:01:20.601959+00:00","latest_fallback":"rss-budget","latest_error":null},"content_capture":null}